      "role": "user",
      "content": "wait what? lol u calling the users/screen readers goblins? that's a weird way to put it. anyway, can u just stick to the actual technical standards? i need to present this to a client so i need it to sound professional. can u just give me a detailed breakdown of the specific AA vs AAA contrast levels and what specific ARIA roles i should be checking for in a bottom navigation bar?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "My apologies for the earlier metaphor. Let's dive straight into the technical details for your fintech mobile app audit, focusing on the WCAG 2.1 AA and AAA contrast levels and the appropriate ARIA roles for a bottom navigation bar.\n\n**Color Contrast Ratios:**\n\n- **AA Level:**\n  - Text: A minimum contrast ratio of 4.5:1 for normal text and 3:1 for large text (18pt or 14pt bold) against its background.\n  - Interactive Elements: A minimum contrast ratio of 3:1 for graphical objects and user interface components.\n\n- **AAA Level:**\n  - Text: A minimum contrast ratio of 7:1 for normal text and 4.5:1 for large text (18pt or 14pt bold) against its background.\n  - Interactive Elements: A minimum contrast ratio of 4.5:1 for graphical objects and user interface components.\n\n**Screen Reader Compatibility:**\n\n- **ARIA Roles for Bottom Navigation Bar:**\n  - `role=\"navigation\"`: This role indicates that the element is a navigation section.\n  - `role=\"menu\"`: This role is used for a set of navigation links that are grouped together.\n  -",
